  "term": "corpus cavernosum",
  "definition": "The corpus cavernosum is erectile tissue whose contractile and relaxation activity is regulated by nitric oxide and the RhoA/Rho-kinase signaling pathway. In the source, impaired relaxation of this tissue is described in diabetic mice along with reduced nitric oxide availability and increased oxidative stress.",
